<title>USA: Georgia jobless rate climbs to 4.9 percent in June.</title>
<headline>Georgia jobless rate climbs to 4.9 percent in June.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia's unemployment rate rose to 4.9 percent in June from 4.1 percent in May, state Labor Commissioner David Poythress said.</p>
<p>That was down from 5.1 percent a year ago.</p>
<p>Poythress attributed much of the monthly increase to the large number of new college graduates looking for work.</p>
<p>Unemployment rates rose during the month for all seven of the state's major metropolitan areas. Their June unemployment rates and their May rates were:</p>
<p>--Albany, 7.1 percent, up from 5.9 percent.</p>
<p>--Athens, 2.9 percent, up from 2.5 percent.</p>
<p>--Atlanta, 4 percent, up from 3.4 percent.</p>
<p>--Augusta, 6.9 percent, up from 5.5 percent.</p>
<p>--Columbus, 5 percent, up from 4.5 percent.</p>
<p>--Macon, 5.2 percent, up from 4.3 percent.</p>
<p>--Savannah, 5.5 percent, up drom 4.4 percent.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
